    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-day owner creation limit: **creating an owner is rejected with 429 once 100 or more owners already carry today's `registrationDate`.**\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing per-city `EnsureCityCapacity` rule), the change is split into small single-responsibility units:\n\n**New repository capability** \u2014 `countByRegistrationDate(LocalDate)` on `OwnerRepository`, implemented in all three arms:\n- `SpringDataOwnerRepository` (`@Query` COUNT, the active `spring-data-jpa` profile)\n- `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl` (JPQL)\n- `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl` (`registration_date = :registrationDate` SQL)\n\n**New pipeline step** \u2014 `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit` counts owners registered today and throws the checked `DailyOwnerLimitException` when the count is \u2265 100 (constant `DAILY_LIMIT`). Wired into `owners.POST.yml` right after `ensureCityCapacity`, in the pre-build validation phase so it runs before any persistence.\n\n**New error handler** \u2014 `DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler` responds `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`, registered via `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DailyOwnerLimitException.yml` (matched most-specific-first, so it takes precedence over the general handlers).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (create 100, expect the 101st to be `429`) passes, and the full build is green.",
